## 5. Controller Logic — What Each File Does

Each controller exports pure async functions that receive `(req, res, next)`. Business logic lives here; no route definitions.

### 5.1 `authController.js`

| Function | Logic |
|----------|-------|
| `register` | Validate body → check duplicate email/username → create User (password auto-hashed by pre-save hook) → generate JWT → return `{ token, user }` |
| `login` | Find user by email (with `+passwordHash` select) → `comparePassword` → generate JWT → return `{ token, user }` |
| `getMe` | `req.user.id` → findById → return user profile |

### 5.2 `userController.js`

| Function | Logic |
|----------|-------|
| `getProfile` | Find User by `:id` → strip private fields → attach follower/following counts (aggregate from Follow) → return |
| `updateProfile` | Verify `req.user.id === :id` → update allowed fields (bio, avatarUrl, profile, tagInterests) → return updated user |
| `getUserPosts` | Find posts by `authorId = :id` → if owner: all posts; if public viewer: only `visibility: public` or anonymous → paginate |
| `getUserCollections` | Same ownership logic → return collections paginated |

### 5.3 `postController.js`

| Function | Logic |
|----------|-------|
| `createPost` | Validate body → resolve tag names to tagIds + tagSlugs (create new Tags if needed, `$inc usageCount`) → create Post → upsert SearchIndex → return post |
| `getPost` | Find by `:id` → if private, check author === req.user → if anonymous, strip `authorId` from response → log analytics "view" event → return |
| `updatePost` | Verify author → update allowed fields → sync SearchIndex → return |
| `deletePost` | Verify author → delete Post → delete related Reactions → delete AnalyticsEvents → delete SearchIndex → `$pull` from all Collections that contained it → `$inc Tag.usageCount(-1)` for each tag |
| `repost` | Create new Post doc with `repostOf = :id`, copy content fields → return |
| `addComment` | Push embedded comment into Post.comments → check 500-comment cap → return updated post |
| `deleteComment` | Verify comment ownership or post ownership → `$pull` comment by `_id` → return |

### 5.4 `followController.js`

| Function | Logic |
|----------|-------|
| `followUser` | Prevent self-follow → create Follow doc → return `201` |
| `unfollowUser` | Delete Follow doc matching `followerId + followeeId` → return `200` |
| `getFollowers` | Find Follow docs where `followeeId = :id` → populate `followerId` with username + avatar → paginate |
| `getFollowing` | Find Follow docs where `followerId = :id` → populate `followeeId` → paginate |

### 5.5 `reactionController.js`

| Function | Logic |
|----------|-------|
| `addReaction` | Upsert Reaction doc → on insert: `$inc Post.reactionCount +1` → return |
| `removeReaction` | Delete Reaction doc → if deleted: `$inc Post.reactionCount -1` → return |
| `getReactions` | Aggregate Reactions for `:postId` grouped by `type` → return `{ like: 12, love: 5, ... }` |

### 5.6 `collectionController.js`

| Function | Logic |
|----------|-------|
| `createCollection` | Create collection with `ownerId = req.user.id` → return |
| `getCollection` | Find by `:id` → if private, verify owner → populate `postIds` with post previews → paginate posts → return |
| `updateCollection` | Verify owner → update name, description, visibility → return |
| `deleteCollection` | Verify owner → delete (do NOT decrement `Post.saveCount` — counts reflect total saves across all collections) |
| `addPost` | Verify owner → `$addToSet postIds` → `$inc postCount +1` → `$inc Post.saveCount +1` → log analytics "save" event → return |
| `removePost` | Verify owner → `$pull postId` → `$inc postCount -1` → `$inc Post.saveCount -1` → return |

### 5.7 `tagController.js`

| Function | Logic |
|----------|-------|
| `listTags` | Optional `?category=` filter → find Tags → sort by name → paginate → return |
| `getTrending` | Find Tags sorted by `usageCount desc` → limit 20 → return |
| `getPostsByTag` | Find Posts where `tagSlugs` contains `:slug` → paginate → return |

### 5.8 `feedController.js`

| Function | Logic |
|----------|-------|
| `getExplore` | Find Posts with `visibility: public` (including anonymous) → sort by `createdAt desc` or `reactionCount desc` based on `?sort=` → paginate → strip authorId from anonymous posts |
| `getFollowingFeed` | Find Follow docs where `followerId = req.user.id` → bulk lookup Posts by those `followeeIds` with `visibility: public` or `followers` → sort by `createdAt desc` → paginate |
| `getTrending` | Aggregate Posts from last 7 days → score by `reactionCount + saveCount + viewCount` → sort desc → limit → return |

### 5.9 `searchController.js`

| Function | Logic |
|----------|-------|
| `search` | Parse `?q=`, `?tag=`, `?user=` → build `$text` query on SearchIndex → filter by `visibility: public` → join back to Post for full data → paginate → return scored results |

### 5.10 `analyticsController.js`

| Function | Logic |
|----------|-------|
| `logEvent` | Create AnalyticsEvent doc (optionally with hashed IP and user agent) → if eventType is "view", `$inc Post.viewCount` → return |
| `getPostAnalytics` | Verify post author === req.user → aggregate AnalyticsEvents by `eventType` for `:postId` → return `{ views, saves, shares, reactions }` |
| `getUserAnalytics` | Find all Posts by user → aggregate AnalyticsEvents for those postIds → sum across all posts → return |

