## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **File upload strategy:** The Post model supports media attachments (`media.url`). Do you want to:
> - (a) Handle file uploads in this backend (using `multer` + local storage or Cloudinary/S3)?
> - (b) Have the frontend upload directly to a cloud service and just send the URL to the API?
> - (c) Skip media uploads for now and only support text posts initially?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Anonymous post identity for comments:** Should anonymous posts allow comments from other users? The current Post model supports it, but we need to decide the UX rule — should the anonymous author be able to reply to comments without revealing their identity?

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
1. **Server boot test**: `npm run dev` starts without errors, connects to MongoDB
2. **Postman collection**: Execute all 38 endpoints following the testing checklist in Section 11
3. **Edge case scripts**: Test duplicate registration, invalid tokens, missing fields, unauthorized access

### Manual Verification
1. Run all Postman tests and verify response status codes and body shapes
2. Check MongoDB Atlas to confirm documents are created/updated/deleted correctly
3. Verify cascade deletes (e.g., deleting a post removes its reactions, analytics, search index entries)
4. Verify denormalized counters stay in sync (reactionCount, saveCount, viewCount)
